/**
@page page_exagrype_PDE-constraints PDE constraints

Off-the-shelf numerical schemes sometimes struggle with numerical relativity.
For example, the Finite Difference schemes have no artificial dissipation,
which is often known to help keep a scheme stable.
Therefore, ExaGRyPE adds bespoke compute kernels, and most of their additional
features can be turned on or off on demand.
For example, the snippet below adds Kreiss-Oliger dissipation:

~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
solver.numerical_scheme = exagrype.api.FD4WithKODissipation(solver, patch_size, rk_order=4, kreiss_oliger_sigma=8.0)
solver.numerical_scheme = exagrype.api.FD4WithKODissipation(solver, patch_size, rk_order=4, kreiss_oliger_sigma=8.0, quantities=["lapse", "shift"])
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

The tutorials provide worked-out examples.


 */
 